## Configuration

Key parameters at the top of `fs_simulation.py`:

| Parameter | Default | Description |
|-----------|---------|-------------|
| `DISK_BLOCKS` | 200 | Total storage blocks |
| `CRITICAL_THRESHOLD` | 0.75 | Fragmentation ratio that triggers alert |
| `BASE_ACCESS_TIME` | 1.0 ms | Baseline file access time |
| `SEEK_PENALTY` | 0.8 ms | Extra delay per additional file extent |
| `MAX_FILE_SIZE` | 20 | Maximum file size in blocks |
| `MIN_FILE_SIZE` | 2 | Minimum file size in blocks |
| `RANDOM_SEED` | 42 | Seed for reproducibility |

---

## Simulation Phases

| Phase | Steps | Behaviour |
|-------|-------|-----------|
| A (warm-up) | 0 – 59 | Save files of varied sizes until ~65% disk utilisation |
| B (fragmentation) | 60 – 199 | Alternate: delete smallest file (punch hole) / save large file |

Phase B is designed to maximally induce fragmentation: small deletions create scattered
free holes that incoming large files must span across multiple extents.

